usive observation returns commit_unknown'","Absence: no stated comparison basis (which field/value) distinguishing desired from conclusive-old from inconclusive"],"finding":"The rule that maps a successful read-back GET result to a disposition (desired vs conclusive-old vs inconclusive) is asserted but never stated — the plan does not say what comparison determines 'desired' (e.g. observed summary equals intended value) versus 'conclusive old state', leaving the executor to infer the classification.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fedc37ef590711a0a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan steps 3-4 / Acceptance Criteria lines 5-7","norm_id":"n1912982f9d2f8d74","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A read-back returns a summary that is neither the intended new value nor the prior value — is that 'old' (replay) or 'inconclusive' (commit_unknown)?"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to step 4 defining the comparison, e.g. 'Classify the read-back by comparing the observed summary to the intended value: exact match => desired (recover); exact match to the pre-write value => conclusive old (replay within budget); any other or failed read => inconclusive (commit_unknown).'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Resolve the max_retries=0 capability assertion against pycontribs/jira #789: confirm that token_auth/PAT (not basic_auth) is unaffected on the pinned jira version, and record that verification in Step 1 / Testing so the guard is grounded in a checked capability rather than an assumption.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 1: 'Construct a dedicated executor client through the pinned public jira.JIRA(..., max_retries=0) argument; fail fast unless _session.max_retries == 0.'","Retrieved source: GitHub pycontribs/jira Issue #789 'max_retries=0 causes authentication error' — 'if max_retries=0, basic authentication will always fail. Oddly, max_retries=0.1 allows basic authentication to succeed, with no retries.'","resolve_symbol confirms jira.JIRA exists in the installed env; summary_executor.py already constructs with token_auth=settings.pat (PAT), which may sidestep the basic-auth-specific bug — but the plan does not state this."],"finding":"The plan's load-bearing capability assertion — that jira.JIRA(..., max_retries=0) safely disables SDK retries and that client._session.max_retries==0 is a reliable guard — is unresolved against known pycontribs/jira behavior. A retrieved upstream issue (pycontribs/jira #789, 'max_retries=0 causes authentication error') reports that with max_retries=0 authentication always fails, and only max_retries=0.1 avoids it. The plan (and code) authenticate via PAT/token_auth rather than basic_auth, so the bug may not apply, but Step 1 / AC line 1 never engage this documented failure mode.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9fe46ab93b840d73","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1; Acceptance Criteria line 1 ('passes max_retries=0 and rejects a nonzero session value')","norm_id":"na96ce841c8f5e032","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Runtime construction of the executor client silently fails auth (or ExecutorClientError fires unexpectedly) on a jira version where max_retries=0 interacts with the auth handshake."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"In Step 1 (or Testing), cite the pinned jira version and state that #789 is basic-auth-specific and does not affect the PAT/token_auth path the executor uses — verified against that version's ResilientSession — or, if it does bite, choose the documented workaround.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"insufficient","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_